      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Don't worry this can happen for vr users as well when trying to grab two objects while manipulating the playspace. \nAt least for now the panic mode needs to stay as it has a purpose, however it should require its own tab in the safety system as to not reset the custom settings. Whoever thought it was a good idea to have a safety setting force changes to other safety settings was clearly not thinking when they implemented it. Panic and custom should not be the same thing. That defeats the whole purpose of having custom settings available to change.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-01-08T18:33:20.028Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So on Desktop as you know hitting Shift F1 - F8 lets you do gestures usually reserved for people with VR, but here's a problem, I like to default go F1 for both arms if I'm not using the others, and F1 is RIGHT NEXT TO ESCAPE. So if I accidentally click Esc instead of F1, I have to reset ALL of my custom Safety settings the way I prefer, and this happens to me OFTEN. Please give it a timed hold of like 3 seconds so accidents stop happening.",
